diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..f1b2912 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,33 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## Page transitions
+
+The shared layout opts into native same-origin view transitions. Browsers without
+support use normal navigation, and reduced-motion preferences disable transitions.
+Critical CSS stays in the document head. Render expectations wait for the masthead
+and the page's `transitionReadyId` (the lead story on news pages, or `main-content`
+by default), without waiting for the footer. These expectations wait for markup,
+not image decoding; lead images load eagerly with high fetch priority and explicit
+dimensions.
+
+There is currently no theme/layout initialization script. If adding one, put it in
+the layout's `head` slot and mark it render-blocking so it executes before the
+incoming transition snapshot:
+
+```astro
+<Layout title="Example">
+  <script slot="head" is:inline type="module" blocking="render">
+    // Small, synchronous theme/layout initialization goes here.
+  </script>
+  <h1>Example</h1>
+</Layout>
+```
+
+Keep analytics and ad scripts non-blocking. Set `transitionReadyId` only to an ID
+that exists on that page, and place it around the initial visible content rather
+than the full article body or later stories.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
